Description: Bump rustix to 1.1.6 in Cargo.lock

Fixes the ppc64le build. On powerpc64(le), rustix uses the libc backend
(no inline asm available), which glob-imports both `libc::*` and the
STATX_* constants from `linux_raw_sys::general`. With libc >= 0.2.185
the libc crate also defines the STATX_* constants on musl >= 1.2.3, so
every `c::STATX_*` reference becomes ambiguous and the build fails with
E0659 on all of them:

    error[E0659]: `STATX_TYPE` is ambiguous
       --> .../rustix-1.1.4/src/fs/statx.rs:75:25

rustix upstream fixed this in 1.1.5 by using an explicit import instead
of a glob (https://github.com/bytecodealliance/rustix/pull/1676,
https://github.com/bytecodealliance/rustix/issues/1675). Other targets
are unaffected: on x86_64/aarch64/riscv64 rustix uses the linux_raw
backend which does not import from libc.

Patch-level bump that keeps the locked dependency versions (all already
satisfied by the existing Cargo.lock entries).

Ref: https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports/-/issues/18492
---
--- a/Cargo.lock
+++ b/Cargo.lock
@@ -3249,9 +3249,9 @@
 
 [[package]]
 name = "rustix"
-version = "1.1.4"
+version = "1.1.6"
 source = "registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"
-checksum = "b6fe4565b9518b83ef4f91bb47ce29620ca828bd32cb7e408f0062e9930ba190"
+checksum = "e5e76742e5294153d4dde1207dbec5bdd81eef6fabdc0d2118babadabfd858aa"
 dependencies = [
  "bitflags 2.11.1",
  "errno",
